      "name": "Body Triangle Entry from Back Control",
      "description": "Start with traditional back control using hooks. Practice transitioning one leg at a time to establish body triangle without losing upper body control. Partner provides progressive resistance (25%, 50%, 75%, then 100%) to simulate realistic entry conditions. Focus on maintaining seatbelt throughout transition and positioning triangle at hip level rather than ribs. Work both sides to develop bilateral proficiency.",
      "duration": "5 minutes per side"
    },
    {
      "name": "Submission Chain Flow Drill",
      "description": "From established body triangle, flow through systematic attack sequence: rear naked choke setup, opponent defends neck, transition to armbar from back, opponent defends arm, switch to triangle from back, opponent escapes triangle angle, return to rear naked choke. Partner provides realistic defensive reactions to each submission attempt. Develop smooth transitions between attacks without releasing triangle lock.",
      "duration": "10 minutes continuous flow"
    },
    {
      "name": "Triangle Retention Against Escape Attempts",
